From 0b21feeeee4155f8badf40b7dc734b11b84bf3cb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: well0nez <well0nez@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 11:21:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 32/82] sunxi: h713: "run fel" reboots into FEL without the
 reset button

Set the vendor's efex flag in RTC GP2 and reset; the SPL answers by
jumping into the BROM's FEL entry. RTC registers sit on a slow clock, so
write until the value reads back and wait a second before the reset - the
vendor writes in a loop and waits 500 ms, and a single store right before
"reset" was lost once in four tries here.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 board/sunxi/hy310.env | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/board/sunxi/hy310.env b/board/sunxi/hy310.env
index 3e5c4500ccd..b79932fb35f 100644
--- a/board/sunxi/hy310.env
+++ b/board/sunxi/hy310.env
@@ -3,6 +3,13 @@
  * The saved environment on a device overrides all of this. Hush expands one
  * level only, so bootargs are assembled where they are used.
  *
+ * "run fel" reboots into FEL without touching the reset button: it sets the
+ * vendor's efex flag in RTC GP2, which our SPL checks first thing and answers
+ * by jumping into the BROM's FEL entry (arch-sunxi/boot0.h, doku/nachtlog/S48).
+ * RTC registers sit on a slow clock: the vendor writes the flag until it reads
+ * back and then waits 500 ms before the watchdog reset. A single store right
+ * before "reset" was lost once in four tries, so do the same here.
+ *
  * h713_project picks the vendor ProjectID_0x*.TSE group; h713_mips_dev and
  * h713_mips_path say where the display artifacts live. These defaults describe
  * the layout this environment boots from (doku/109): the artifacts sit in
@@ -29,4 +36,5 @@ boot_net=
 	setenv bootargs "${bootargs_base} root=/dev/nfs rw nfsroot=${serverip}:${nfsroot},vers=3,tcp ip=dhcp";
 	tftpboot 0x60000000 ${serverip}:${bootfile};
 	bootm 0x60000000
+fel=while itest.l *0x07090108 != 0x5aa5a55a; do mw.l 0x07090108 0x5aa5a55a; done; sleep 1; reset
 bootcmd=h713_disp init ${h713_project}; run boot_${h713_boot}; run boot_net
